{"agent_id":"pp3g-kifs-investigate-session-history-divergence-419-under-epic","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-23T18:47:38.346925914Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0b35f3d4-0eba-4cee-a61b-205c6778a36c","comment_uuid":"5d0b939b-b478-409f-9689-703c143fa695","author":"pp3g-kifs-investigate-session-history-divergence-419-under-epic","content":"FINDINGS (read-only forensics; each DB + -wal/-shm copied to /tmp/opencode/w3 BEFORE querying; originals never opened; timestamps UTC from ms-epoch columns).\n\n[1] SCHEMA: all three DBs share one v2 SQLite lineage (project/project_directory/session/message/part/session_message/todo/workspace/event...). opencode-fork-pp3g.db and opencode-local.db carry an IDENTICAL 38-migration set. opencode.db now carries 45 (see [4]).\n\n[2] PER-DB PER-PROJECT STATS.\n- opencode.db (main): 698 sessions, span 2026-06-21 17:55 -> 2026-08-09 03:51:11 (max time_updated). By project: tripn-astro 457 (->Aug 9 03:51), ASES 161 (Jun 23 00:55 -> Aug 9 02:52), global 29, crosslink 21, Tools 4, others <=5. ~70 ASES .worktrees/pp3g-* directories registered under the ASES project, latest registration Aug 9 02:23 - NONE later.\n- opencode-fork-pp3g.db: 539 sessions, span 2026-08-06 01:34 -> NOW (my own dispatch session ses_fd01eb5a... titled 'Investigating session-history divergence (#419)' is in here). ASES project: 251 sessions = 22 directly under /home/claude-code/projects/ASES (Aug 9 02:38 -> today 18:22) + the rest across dozens of pp3g-* worktree dirs (Aug 6 -> today). 'global' 154 = /tmp harness dirs (matrix-run etc.), not ASES.\n- opencode-local.db: 77 sessions, ALL on 2026-08-06 (01:46 -> 13:24). Projects: /tmp/opencode/fork-build 16, ASES worktree pp3g-Nu9v 45, global 16. NO table shows any content change after Aug 6 13:24 despite file mtime Aug 18 14:52.\n\n[3] PROJECT IDENTITY: ASES = project id b826eb8e3de2d318e0aee6d50cbe1ac2270ad673 in ALL THREE DBs; directory keying consistent (/home/claude-code/projects/ASES registered in each). Worktree subdirs were keyed under the same project id, not separate identities.\n\n[4] BINARY TOPOLOGY + TODAY'S EVENT. PATH 'opencode' is a bash wrapper (mtime Aug 9 00:47, fail-closed fork guard #274/#154) exec'ing node_modules/opencode-ai/bin/opencode.exe, which reports '1.18.13-pp3g-fork' (verified via --version under an isolated fake HOME). Stock 1.18.13 preserved at fork-backups/20260808-233133/opencode.exe.stock-1.18.13 and bin/opencode.exe.stock-20260808-234726. The fork writes its OWN db file (opencode-fork-pp3g.db) inside the SHARED ~/.local/share/opencode/ dir. TODAY Aug 23 17:27 @opencode-ai/cli 0.0.0-beta-17963 ('OpenCode 2.0 preview', command opencode2) was installed (symlink mtime 17:27); at exactly 17:27:49 main opencode.db received 7 pending upstream migrations in one burst: loose_psylocke(0804), import_legacy_credentials(0805), workspace_domain(0808), execution_claim_attempts(0811), session_inbox(0812), worktree(0812), session_viewed_state(0819). These 7 exist ONLY in main db - the fork build predates them, so the fork cannot have applied them.\n\n[5] V2 STORE INTERNALS: opencode2 added tables session_v2/worktree/kv/session_inbox/session_pending/instruction_*. session_v2 contains the 698 migrated legacy rows PLUS EXACTLY ONE new session: ses_fd043424cffeoF2uQ4EDzj8nB1 'opencode 2 session-start docs', directory=/home/claude-code/projects/ASES, created today 17:48, updated 18:31 - i.e., the operator's own active opencode2 session. Legacy 'session' table untouched since Aug 9.\n\n[6] CUTOVER NARRATIVE: the last ASES sessions ever written to main db ARE the install tasks ('Atomic install 3B/3C: replace + wrapper flip', Aug 8 23:47-23:49). Sessions updating up to 03:51 Aug 9 are pre-cutover-created ones flushing final updates. First fork-db sessions in the ASES main dir: 'Crosslink guard issue investigation' 02:38, 'Investigating session loss and slow performance' 03:04 Aug 9 - the operator was already chasing this on day one.\n\nWHY: every claim above is a direct probe result (SQL aggregates over copied DBs, file mtimes, --version under fake HOME). HOW CERTAIN: evidence-based throughout. WHAT-NOT-TESTED: opencode2 source-level db-path selection; behavior of live binaries against real HOME (deliberately avoided - read-only constraint).","created_at":"2026-08-23T18:47:38.339815138Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:5P0In62Vy+f5W70LFsnSXIcxGCYCn9lXy8xFYykiUP4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxSAAMdbb+YlemhsxAjiKxl34uM/C3uMkJNfJ812YnugAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAl3BIGQKDZ5AHi+M2xpqGSsmLzcNU+aOR6h0JqT9XzOyLsAa0/UWEONyOqx59TcGcy4JQjuw7Xuy196KRYWRfBg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:5P0In62Vy+f5W70LFsnSXIcxGCYCn9lXy8xFYykiUP4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxSAAMdbb+YlemhsxAjiKxl34uM/C3uMkJNfJ812YnugAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIHzAvGfq3+W+zSpC/TwltahkaxHFAi3GbMa+V3qlzrgNg1BidmxlFiJ9FVQSKbAVK6C75/lRDJuIhPJI+3xcwY="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-kifs-investigate-session-history-divergence-419-under-epic","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-08-23T18:48:17.432431939Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0b35f3d4-0eba-4cee-a61b-205c6778a36c","comment_uuid":"6d7c334d-102d-4449-8aba-e2153d43d683","author":"pp3g-kifs-investigate-session-history-divergence-419-under-epic","content":"RESULT — ROOT CAUSE (ranked) + FIX OPTIONS.\n\nRANK 1 (primary, confirmed): STORE SPLIT BY BINARY BRAND AT THE AUG 8-9 CUTOVER = baseline hypothesis (c). WHY: since the wrapper flip (Aug 9 00:47) every 'opencode' invocation execs the pp3g fork, which persists sessions ONLY to opencode-fork-pp3g.db; the viewing surface that shows 'frozen' history is opencode2 (OpenCode 2.0 preview, installed today 17:27), which reads/migrates ONLY ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db. All Aug 9->23 work (539 fork-db sessions, incl. all crosslink agent traffic and 22 ASES-main-dir sessions) is invisible to it; newest non-opencode2 row there is Aug 9 03:51 - exactly the reported freeze. WHAT: migration-burst/install-minute correlation (17:27 == 17:27:49), --version probes under fake HOME, per-day session histograms (main: 119 on Aug 8 -> 2 on Aug 9 -> 0; fork: continuous Aug 6->today), identical project ids across DBs. HOW CERTAIN: evidence-based (high). WHAT-NOT-TESTED: opencode2's source-level db-path derivation; whether any env/config can redirect either binary to another store; viewer listing semantics inside opencode2 (exact directory-match vs project-scope).\n\nRANK 2 (amplifier, benign): baseline hypothesis (a) variant - the viewing surface reads a store that stopped RECEIVING writes on Aug 9. NOT data loss: the v1 JSON store is gone (storage/ holds only marker byte '2'), but all v1-era data was migrated into main db and survives intact (698 rows, now projected into session_v2 by today's migration).\n\nRANK 3 (refuted): baseline hypothesis (b) project-key drift. Same project id b826eb8e... for ASES in all three DBs; consistent directory mapping. No identity split exists at the data level.\n\nOPENCODE-LOCAL.DB IDENTITY: throwaway store of the Aug 6 LOCAL FORK BUILD/TEST run (project dir /tmp/opencode/fork-build; schema byte-identical in migrations to fork db; all content confined to Aug 6 01:46-13:24). It went cold because that build was superseded by the durable rebuild installed Aug 8 23:31-23:49. The Aug 18 14:52 mtime bump with ZERO content delta in any table is best explained as an open-and-checkpoint/metadata touch (e.g., a tool briefly opening it); no write occurred. HOW CERTAIN: identity evidence-based; mtime explanation guess. WHAT-NOT-TESTED: process logs for Aug 18 (none kept).\n\nFIX OPTIONS (ranked):\nA. MERGE (durable fix): one-time ATTACH of a fork-db copy into main db; INSERT OR IGNORE session/message/part/session_message/todo rows (project ids already match so FKs hold). CAVEATS: main db now runs the NEWER 45-migration schema with parallel tables (session AND session_v2; fork lacks session_v2) - rows likely need dual-projection into both tables; do it with ALL binaries stopped, after backup, prototyped entirely on copies first. Effort M / risk M.\nB. READ-SIDE UNION (immediate): small read-only tool or scheduled export that unions both stores for listing/archaeology; zero risk to live stores; does not fix the native viewer. Effort S-M / risk S.\nC. FORWARD-CANONICALIZE: declare main db/opencode2 canonical going forward and route new work there IF a db-path override exists (UNVERIFIED - would need a config probe); keep fork-db as archived history readable via sqlite. Effort S / risk S; leaves an Aug 9-23 hole in the native timeline unless combined with A.\nD. DO NOTHING STRUCTURAL: use 'opencode2 export'/sqlite reads ad hoc. Effort XS / permanent friction.\nRECOMMENDATION: B now to unblock verification needs; spike A on copies (schema map session->session_v2) before any live merge.\n\nPROCESS NOTES: constraints honored - no repo file changes, no commits, originals never opened, scratch only under /tmp/opencode/w3/. Per dispatch CONSTRAINTS ('NO crosslink sync - state audit comes later') I did NOT run crosslink sync despite boilerplate instructions to sync after each checkpoint; these comments are local until the operator syncs. Session-work lock reported stale (known noise) and was left alone.\n\nMODEL CAPABILITY OBSERVATIONS (ox-alpha-free / opencode-go ox-alpha-free; first routing-matrix entry, n=1 anecdote): launch via crosslink kickoff clean on first try; stale-lock warning did not impede; full 3-DB forensic pass (~25 tool calls incl. 5.4GB of DB copies, sqlite aggregation over 2.6-2.8GB stores, two webfetches) completed in ~30 min wall with zero retries, zero denials, zero rate-limit symptoms; one SQL error (event table has no time_created) self-corrected immediately without looping; long outputs (>70 rows) handled without truncation problems. HOW CERTAIN: single-run observation, not a benchmark.","created_at":"2026-08-23T18:48:17.425843950Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:5P0In62Vy+f5W70LFsnSXIcxGCYCn9lXy8xFYykiUP4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxSAAMdbb+YlemhsxAjiKxl34uM/C3uMkJNfJ812YnugAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA6iA1Q+y0DKyacbXQtQych+FSv5EJyRDSqICrIb6dGyBrJrO1OxqEPdMLkYksKvPIRFGKcZx/tajDFht7UN06DA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:5P0In62Vy+f5W70LFsnSXIcxGCYCn9lXy8xFYykiUP4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxSAAMdbb+YlemhsxAjiKxl34uM/C3uMkJNfJ812YnugAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFk2R47sKS0+hIjj1y3tVUxBV9YkI8N50zzgn2p4BCQgWNJBMiRlocnbFImpeKUvfHHSq+RXE0/AX4s+r8/HuwI="}
